  "about": "Guild positions (issue #103): the first makes guild PosTest and invites the second (RUSTNAROK_CLIENT_GUILD=accept). On the members page the master picks 'Position 2' from the second's drop-down and presses OK (issue #516); both windows follow and the title under the second's name follows (ZC_GUILD_POSITION). On the positions page (issue #519: the cell grid, edits in place, one OK) the master ticks Invite on positions 1 and 2, renames 1 'Officer' and sets its tax to 10, and OK sends them in one packet; the member sees the page read-only; the master writes the notice on the Announcement tab and Send gives the second '[ Hi ]' and '[ Welcome ]'; the second's window and the title follow. The second leaves from their own row on the members page (asked first); the first sees them go. @breakguild ends it. Both characters must start without a guild or clan. If a run stops between the invitation and leaving, the second stays in PosTest and the next run fails at the invitation: log in as the second, leave from the members page, then @breakguild as the first (the scenario reset can't take a member out of a guild).",
